{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>While My glory passes by.</b> When I pass before you." "<b>In the cleft of the rock.</b> As in ״הָעֵינֵי הָאֲנָשִׁים הָהֵם תְּנַקֵּר״ (Numbers 16), ״יִקְּרוּהָ עֹרְבֵי נַחַל״ (Proverbs 30), ״אֲנִי קַרְתִּי וְשָׁתִיתִי מַיִם״ (II Kings 19:24; Isaiah 37:25) — they share one root: נִקְרַת הַצּוּר: cutting of the rock." "<b>And I will cover you with My hand.</b> From here that permission was given to the destructive forces to harm. And its Targum: ״וְאָגֵין בְּמֵימְרִי״ — it is a reverent euphemism for the One above, who does not need to cover him with an actual hand."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:26.656421797Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}